{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bezout Identity for Polynomials.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bezout Identity for Polynomials.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bezout identity for polynomials bezout identity for polynomials","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bezout Identity for Polynomials.md","fileName":"Bezout Identity for Polynomials.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bezout Identity for Polynomials","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:45\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Polynomial Algorithms and Elimination]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial Algorithms and Elimination","Field","Coprime Polynomials","Polynomial Resultant","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bezout Identity for Polynomials.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bezout Identity for Polynomials.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bezout identity for polynomials bezout identity for polynomials","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bezout Identity for Polynomials.md","fileName":"Bezout Identity for Polynomials.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bezout Identity for Polynomials","heading":"Bezout Identity for Polynomials","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"If polynomials f₁,…,fₙ over a [[Field]] are coprime, there are polynomials g₁,…,gₙ such that f₁g₁ + ··· + fₙgₙ = 1. Their generated ideal is therefore the whole polynomial ring.\n\nThe identity follows from the fact that every one-variable polynomial ideal is principal. It certifies [[Coprime Polynomials]] and supports the common-factor interpretation of a [[Polynomial Resultant]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial Algorithms and Elimination","Field","Coprime Polynomials","Polynomial Resultant","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full